WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.683
A game with an edge:

2
00:00:01.683 --> 00:00:05.416
half the trades bring 1.2 times the risk, half lose one.

3
00:00:05.416 --> 00:00:07.082
The Kelly criterion says:

4
00:00:07.082 --> 00:00:11.748
risk about eight percent of capital, and growth is fastest on average.

5
00:00:11.748 --> 00:00:17.281
More than that and growth slows, and at around two Kelly capital typically shrinks,

6
00:00:17.281 --> 00:00:19.814
even though every trade is profitable.

7
00:00:20.814 --> 00:00:25.324
The simulator plays out a thousand futures of 200 trades each.

8
00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:28.671
At two and four percent risk there is no ruin.

9
00:00:28.671 --> 00:00:34.709
At Kelly, two percent of the futures went broke; at 15 percent risk, 28; at 25, 74.

10
00:00:34.709 --> 00:00:38.346
And in real life the edge is not known in advance,

11
00:00:38.346 --> 00:00:41.838
so practitioners bet half or a quarter of Kelly.
